      "content": "I agree with you; relying on school prestige or specific company names for \"leadership presence\" can indeed introduce unconscious bias and overlook equally qualified candidates. We must strictly evaluate leadership capability through behavioral examples rather than educational pedigree since a degree from Morehouse or Howard demonstrates dedication and discipline just as effectively as any Ivy League school. For the hiring process, I suggest standardizing the weighting of resume attributes to focus solely on verified outcomes like team size scaled or budget managed, ensuring the assessment remains blind to Alma Mater. This approach ensures fairness where a senior engineer from any institution is judged purely on their proven ability to lead culture and deliver results.",
